course: dictionary
lesson: 12101
title: Cogent arguments
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Cogent is a formal word. It means clear, logical and convincing. A cogent argument gives good reasons, one after another, and those reasons make people agree. You will meet it in debates, persuasive writing and exams.
explain: Look for the clues. «We should have longer lunch breaks, because we get tired in the afternoon, and a rest helps us learn.» The word because links the reason to the claim, so the argument is cogent. Ask yourself: does each point lead clearly to the next?
explain: Cogent does not mean loud or long. A short argument can be cogent if it is clear and sensible. Everyday English often says «convincing» or «strong» instead, so if you meet cogent, try swapping in one of those words and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Cogent means clear, logical and convincing.
fact: Cogent is an adjective, and its comparative form is more cogent.
fact: A cogent argument gives clear reasons and evidence that make people agree.
fact: «Her cogent reason for staying in made the whole class agree.»
fact: Convincing and strong are everyday words that can often replace cogent.
exercise: «Her cogent reason for staying in was that the rain was heavy and the roads were closed.» What does cogent mean? | Lost and confused | Short and rude | *Clear, logical and convincing | Loud and cheerful
exercise: Ravi says, «My argument is cogent because I have three facts to back it up.» Which word is a good swap for cogent? | Quiet | Silly | *Convincing | Hungry
exercise: Which is a cogent argument? | *"We should recycle, because plastic harms sea animals, and recycling cuts the plastic we throw away." | "Because I said so." | "Pizza is best because it is yummy."
test: Which sentence gives a cogent reason? | "I like dogs, so dogs are the best." | "Dogs are nice." | *"Dogs need daily walks, because they have lots of energy, and a walk stops them getting bored."
test: What is the best opposite of cogent? | *Muddled | Convincing | Strong | Clear
exam: «The team's cogent plan won the vote because each step was clear and sensible.» Which word is closest in meaning to cogent? | Late | *Convincing | Quiet | Foolish
